Context: Web challenge 'Sign Kudasai' - JWT issuer/validator; cannot issue token for username=admin. Goal: retrieve ICC{} flag.

Confirmed vulns report:
1) JWT verification bypass via ignored ParseWithClaims errors and wrong signature sentinel. In /verify, code only rejects jwt.ErrTokenUnverifiable and jwt.ErrSignatureInvalid (incorrect sentinel in v5; should be ErrTokenSignatureInvalid). Any other parse/validation error is ignored; claims.Username may be populated via json.Unmarshal even when parse returns error, so username=admin is trusted and flag is returned. Exploit: craft token with payload {"username":"admin","exp":"x"} (exp wrong type), any signature; send to /verify?token=...; expect flag.
2) Expired JWTs accepted because token.Valid not checked and ErrTokenExpired ignored. Not needed for flag but confirms lax verification.

Task: Provide a concrete exploitation plan to obtain the flag remotely, including request(s) to make and token structure. If anything is missing, state exactly what additional info is required.



